Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sub-decomposes Renderer::flip()'s W20A `phase=total` window into 5 named
sub-buckets + 1 derived residual covering the regions OUTSIDE W20A's
drain / dirty / present / housekeeping brackets — i.e. the ~12 ms / flip
/ 32% unmeasured slice identified in iter K residual decomp as the
dominant unmeasured cost post-slot-0117.

Brackets:
  fb_setup            — flip() entry block before the W20A dirty bracket
                        opens (lines ~3658→3729). Local-variable book-
                        keeping + _inter_flip_ms calc + diff prelude.
                        Hypothesis: <0.1 ms (mostly local stores).
  fb_prev_frame_blit  — prev-frame surface alloc/destroy on dim/format
                        mismatch + SDL_BlitSurface cache→prev (76800 byte
                        INDEX8 copy). Dormant when PREVFRAME_DIFF=OFF
                        (default since wave 17.6 patch 0085); bracket
                        exists for self-validation + future
                        PREVFRAME_DIFF=1 ablation comparison.
  fb_yield            — SDL_Delay(0) cooperative-thread yield to SDL3
                        audio thread. SUSPECT for the dominant 12 ms
                        slice per audio_mix_zero_is_not_audio_off.md +
                        audio_cost_attribution_unknown.md — cooperative
                        scheduler attributes audio wall-clock to the
                        main thread's flip() call. Hypothesis: 1-12 ms.
  fb_diag_logs        — flip_failed log + per-10-flips flip-probe
                        LOG_INFO emit + drawcalls reset. Per-line fsync
                        per patch 0036; spikes on per-10 emit flips.
                        Hypothesis: amortized ~0.05-0.2 ms / flip.
  fb_audit_flushes    — 7 _maybe_flush_*_audit() calls + flip-inner
                        accumulator close + W20A sample-array fill
                        block. Each _maybe_flush_* early-returns 99/100
                        and emits 1-3 LOG_INFO lines on 1/100.
                        Hypothesis: amortized ~0.1-0.5 ms / flip.
  fb_residual         — derived. _flip_inner_dt_ns − (W20A named sum +
                        sum(fb_*)); clamped at 0. Self-validation:
                        small median (<1 ms) ⇒ brackets exhaustive;
                        large residual surfaces an unbracketed chunk
                        for wave-29.

Implementation pattern: inline `if (_flip_body_instr_on)` guards with
explicit Uint64 t0 captures (mirrors W20A's existing flip()-side pattern;
NOT the RAII pattern used by game.cpp's W22A/W22.5 instrumentation —
contract § 4 explicitly forbids mixing patterns in this file).

Per-flip cost when env unset: ~10 conditional branches + 1 cached
static-const-bool read (sub-µs total). Will not measurably regress fps
in the W28A2 control PLAY (must match iter L baseline 34.33 fps within
~1 fps tolerance).

Storage: 6 × 100 × 8 = ~5 KB static state for the sample arrays + 1
shared idx (each bucket fills exactly once per flip).

`_flip_inner_dt_ns` hoisted from inner-block scope to flip()-function
scope so the residual block can read it after the fb_audit_flushes
bracket close (was previously scoped inside `{ ... }` and invisible
after the brace).

Emit site: _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit() in Renderer.cpp, AFTER the
W20A `[flip-stat]` block and BEFORE the W20B `[engine-tick-stat]` block.
Output ordering: outermost-to-innermost (flip-stat → flip-body-stat →
engine-tick-stat → mode-tick-stat → mode-draw-scene-stat → mds-* →
counters). Distinct prefix `flip-body-stat` so the 7-layer grep stays
clean. Empty-block placeholder lines (`n=0`, all numerics 0.00) emitted
when env is set but no samples landed (e.g. first audit-flush after
enable) so per-block log shape stays uniform 6 lines.

Coupling note: residual reads W20A-populated `_drain_ns` / `_dirty_ns` /
`_present_ns` / `_hk_ns` locals. Without `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FLIP_INSTR=1`
those stay 0 and residual computes as `total - sum(fb_*)` which is
still meaningful but no longer apples-to-apples with W20A's named
phases. Operator iter sets both hints together.

Direct-VESA-aware gating per direct_vesa_aware_instrumentation_gating.md:
gate counter = `_flip_total` (already ticking; fires regardless of which
SDL flush path is engaged). Emit fields = per-flip dt locals (no
internal sticky-state). Verified clean against the two W23/W23.7 traps.

Strict-"1" match: only literal `1` activates; any other value (unset,
empty, "0") is OFF.

Workspace-local; never upstreamed.

See docs/PHASE11-WAVE-28-CONTRACT.md for the full bracket-scheme
rationale + § 10 wave-29 decision tree.
